udit storage. 2) Check reads are limited by role. 3) Check redaction rules apply to sensitive fields. 4) Answer no if read access is broad (`*`, all engineers) or no redaction exists.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"E11.3\",\n  \"check\": \"Integrity protection (hash chain, signatures, or WORM) plus sequence numbers or delivery receipts let missing records be detected, with an alert on gaps or pipeline failure.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Open the audit writer and store config. 2) Check for integrity protection (hash chain, signatures, or WORM) plus sequence numbers or delivery receipts. 3) Check an alert fires on gaps or pipeline failure. 4) Answer no if any piece is missing, or a hash is computed but never verified.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"E11.4\",\n  \"check\": \"High-impact actions are blocked when required audit capture is down.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find high-impact action paths. 2) Check they confirm audit capture is working before the action runs. 3) Answer no if audit write errors are caught and the action proceeds, or the audit record is written only after success.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8c561077-96df-4d9c-ad99-669be22cb1e5","uuid":"f320e76f-bb76-4cad-b717-9d3f9389ece0","timestamp":"2026-10-20T12:56:56.093Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"src/tools/executor.ts:3:import { audit, AuditUnavailable, redactPhi } from \"../audit/recorder.js\";\nsrc/tools/executor.ts:88:    const safe = redactPhi(raw);\nsrc/audit/recorder.ts:83:export function redactPhi(value: unknown): unknown {\nsrc/audit/recorder.ts:87:  if (Array.isArray(value)) return value.map(redactPhi);\nsrc/audit/recorder.ts:92:      out[k] = redactPhi(v);\n---\nk8s/deployment.yaml:8:    pod-security.kubernetes.io/audit: restricted\nREADME.md:19:| Tool executor | `src/tools/executor.ts` | allowlist, kill switch, budgets, approvals, audi